    "label": "Honors Program",
    "notes": "To receive School Honors, students must complete all upper-division courses in the major with an overall grade-point average of 3.5 or better. For highest School Honors, students must also complete a senior thesis. The senior thesis may be satisfied by completing either Public Health 198 or a departmental 198 course. The 198 course may not be counted as an elective course toward the major and must be supervised by an Academic Senate faculty member from the school. Highest honors is awarded if the faculty sponsor deems the work superior.",
